    "result_text": "Confirmed working end-to-end. The `/api/clients` endpoint returns all clients when `q` is absent (so the projects page's bare fetch is unaffected) and filters case-insensitively when `q` is present.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request \u2014 \"a box to search for a client by name\" \u2014 is implemented as a small, additive full-stack change. The Playwright spec passes (`1 passed`).\n\n**Database** (`V6__client_name_index.sql`) \u2014 new Flyway migration adding an index on `client(name)` to keep name lookups fast as the list grows.\n\n**Server**\n- `ClientRepository` \u2014 added `findByNameContainingIgnoreCaseOrderByIdAsc(term)` (case-insensitive name match, stable id order).\n- `ClientsGet` \u2014 now takes an optional `@HttpQueryParameter(\"q\")`; blank/absent returns every client (unchanged behavior for existing callers like the projects page), otherwise returns the narrowed list. Verified both paths by curl.\n\n**Front-end** (all additive, following the app's slot/URL/query rules)\n- `slots/defs/clientsToolbar.ts` \u2014 new `clients.toolbar` slot region.\n- `features/clients/search.slot.tsx` \u2014 the `client-search` box, a self-contained file that owns the `clientSearch` URL search param (a filter outlives a click \u2192 URL, not `useState`).\n- `ClientsPage.tsx` \u2014 reads the same URL key, folds it into the `['clients', q]` query key (still prefix-matched by existing `invalidateQueries(['clients'])`), fetches `/api/clients?q=...`, and mounts `<ClientsToolbar.Slot />` above the table.\n\nThe search box and the list share only a URL key and a query key \u2014 no imports or callbacks between them. `data-testid` anchors (`client-search`, `client-row-*`, `client-name`) match the spec exactly, and no existing testids were renamed. No pinned scaffolding or the spec was touched.",
